WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.875
Environmental conditions can become harder to recognize after sunset.

00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:07.480
Wind shifts may be less visible, temperature may fall, and fog or mist can form.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.145
Humidity and condensation can affect lenses, sensors, electronics, and image quality.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.890
Cold night temperatures can reduce battery performance and usable flight time.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.225
Plan with larger reserves, follow approved battery-temperature guidance,

00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:22.360
and monitor actual consumption rather than assuming daylight endurance.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.880
Fog, mist, precipitation,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.605
and haze reduce visibility and can scatter aircraft or ground lighting.

00:00:27.605 --> 00:00:31.340
A light may remain visible even when the surrounding obstacles and flight path are not.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.865
Visibility must support the whole operation, not just sight of one beacon.

00:00:34.865 --> 00:00:37.860
Wires, trees, poles, towers, building edges, cranes,

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.000
and vehicles can blend into dark backgrounds.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.265
Temporary obstacles and people may appear after the site review.

00:00:43.265 --> 00:00:46.390
Obstacle sensors may miss thin or poorly illuminated features.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.320
Launch and recovery areas need stable footing, clear boundaries, sufficient light,

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.865
and control of people and vehicles.

00:00:51.865 --> 00:00:55.795
Protect crew night vision while making the landing surface and hazards identifiable.

00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:57.370
Prepare an alternate recovery area.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.008
Monitor changes throughout the flight.

00:00:59.008 --> 00:01:03.255
If temperature, wind, moisture, visibility, obstacles, or activity reduce margins,

00:01:03.255 --> 00:01:04.089
return early.

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:08.730
A safe cancellation or shortened mission is better than discovering a night hazard during

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:09.600
a low-battery landing.
